{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.WedderburnConstruction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.WedderburnConstruction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Matrix.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Combinatorics.Enumerative.Partition","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Common","lean:module:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Hoefsmit","lean:module:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Wedderburn"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Wedderburn.wedderburnEmbedOf_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Wedderburn.wedderburnEmbedOf_injective","kind":"theorem","line":230,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/WedderburnConstruction.lean#L230-L238","doc":"And it is injective, so it deserves the name \"embedding\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Wedderburn.wedderburnEmbedOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Wedderburn.wedderburnEmbedOf","kind":"def","line":222,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/WedderburnConstruction.lean#L222-L228","doc":"**The Wedderburn embedding, given RSK.** This is what the former\n`opaque wedderburnEmbed` was axiomatised to be — now a definition, with its one\nhypothesis named. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Wedderburn.regIndexEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Wedderburn.regIndexEquiv","kind":"def","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/WedderburnConstruction.lean#L217-L220","doc":"Given RSK, the regular index is equivalent to `Fin (n!)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Wedderburn.RSKDimIdentity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Wedderburn.RSKDimIdentity","kind":"def","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/WedderburnConstruction.lean#L165-L215","doc":"**The one missing ingredient**, written down instead of assumed: the\nRobinson–Schensted–Knuth dimension identity `Σ_λ (f^λ)² = n!`. Everything above\nis independent of it; everything below is explicitly conditional on it.\n\n⚠ **This is not a new statement.** The corpus already carries it as\n`QOU.BraidKnot.OVTopAssembly.sum_numSYT_sq_eq_factorial`.\n\n**Status corrected 2026-09-06 (bean `qou-1knw`).** This paragraph used to quote\n`scripts/lean-axiom-guard.py` recording that declaration as `sorryAx` under\n\"known-BAD: the RSK identity and everything reindexed from it\". That entry was\n**a month out of date**, and the guard could not say so because it had been\nunable to run at all — it exits 2 when any olean in its cone is missing or\nstale, and ~104 of its modules were. Once rebuilt, the guard reported a\npromotion: that declaration and three siblings measure exactly\n`[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]`.\n\nIt still carries `[SnIsotypicSpechtSplit ℚ]`, so the older caveat about the\n§3b-cond pattern was the right thing to worry about — but that binder now has an\ninstance, itself clean, so the statement is established rather than merely\nconditional. The instance is built **from** `QOU.Mathlib.rskBurnsideHolds`, so\nthe declaration is derivative and citing it as the *source* of the identity would\nbe circular.\n\nSo *that* declaration is available only conditionally, and `RSKDimIdentity`\nstates the same obligation **as an explicit hypothesis on the theorem** rather\nthan inside an ambient class binder — which is the difference the guard is\ncomplaining about.\n\n✅ **DISCHARGED 2026-09-05 (bean `qou-yos9`) — and the paragraph above cited the\nwrong declaration.** The corpus carries a *second*, independent route:\n`QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedRSKBurnside.lean:56` proves\n`rskBurnsideHolds (n : ℕ) : RSKBurnsideHolds n` universally, from\n`Schensted.rskEquiv` over a ~48-module in-repo Schensted development. Measured\nafter building that cone (46 ok, 2 up-to-date, 0 errors), `rskBurnsideHolds`,\n`card_pairs_eq_sum` and `rskEquiv` each report exactly\n`[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]` — no `sorryAx`, no class binder. And\n`RSKDimIdentity n` is *definitionally* `RSKBurnsideHolds n`, since\n`seminormalDim = QOU.Mathlib.dimSYT` and `heckeDim n = n.factorial` are both\ndefinitions, so the discharge is that theorem applied and nothing else.\n\n`QOU/HeckeAlgebra/WedderburnUnconditional.lean` carries it, along with\n`wedderburnEmbedTotal` — injective with no axiom and no hypothesis. The\n`numSYT` ↔ `dimSYT` bridge this docstring said would be needed\n(`QOU/BraidKnot/SYTEncodingBridge.lean`) is **not** on that route and was never\nrequired.\n\nEverything in this module stays stated over the hypothesis. The hypothesis form\nis what makes the dependency legible, and the discharge is one import away for\nany caller that wants it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Wedderburn.card_regIndex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Wedderburn.card_regIndex","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/WedderburnConstruction.lean#L158-L163","doc":"`Fintype.card (RegIndex n) = Σ_λ (f^λ)²` — the quantity RSK identifies with\n`n!`, computed rather than assumed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Wedderburn.blockDiagonal_trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Wedderburn.blockDiagonal_trace","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/WedderburnConstruction.lean#L125-L156","doc":"**The regular-representation trace formula.** `blockDiagonal` places block\n`λ` along the diagonal once for each multiplicity index `m : Fin (f^λ)`, so its\ntrace weights each block trace by `f^λ`:\n\n    trace (blockDiagonal x) = Σ_λ f^λ · trace (x λ)\n\nUnconditional — no RSK, no positivity. This is the identity\n`QOU/HeckeAlgebra/MarkovTrace.lean`'s module doc used to advertise for\n`wenzlBridge` and which nothing proved, because until `blockDiagonal` existed\nthere was no embedding to state it over.\n\nIt is also a check on the construction rather than only a lemma about it: had\nthe multiplicity been mis-indexed in `blockDiagonal`, the coefficient here would\ncome out `1` or `(f^λ)²` and the proof would not close. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Wedderburn.blockDiagonal_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Wedderburn.blockDiagonal_injective","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/WedderburnConstruction.lean#L92-L123","doc":"**The assembly is injective — it is an embedding.** Two decompositions with\nthe same block-diagonal matrix agree block by block, read off at multiplicity\nindex `0`, which exists because `0 < f^λ`.\n\nThe positivity is taken as an explicit argument rather than invoked, and that is\ndeliberate — though the reason first given for it was about the container, and\nthat part is now wrong. Discharge it with\n\n    blockDiagonal_injective (fun lam => Hoefsmit.seminormalDim_pos' lam)\n\n**Corrected 2026-09-05 (bean `qou-kp2z`).** This docstring said the container's\nrestored olean snapshot \"carries only the older `seminormalDim_pos`\", so\n`seminormalDim_pos'` was unavailable. That was true when measured and is no\nlonger true: `Hoefsmit.olean` in the snapshot was ~3 months stale, and any\n`scripts/lean-direct-cone.sh` run touching this module rebuilds it from source,\nafter which `seminormalDim_pos'` is present. The claim described a *repairable\ncache state* as if it were a fixed property of the environment — see\n`QOU/HeckeAlgebra/WedderburnTrace.lean` for what that staleness cost elsewhere.\n\nThe hypothesis stays explicit anyway, for the reason that does not expire:\n`seminormalDim_pos` takes a `0 < n` that the statement does not need (the empty\ndiagram has exactly one standard tableau), and bolting on a decoy hypothesis to\nsatisfy a cache is the shape `scripts/lean-decoy-hypothesis-audit.py` exists to\ncatch. Naming the real hypothesis is right whether or not the cache is fresh. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Wedderburn.blockDiagonal_same","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Wedderburn.blockDiagonal_same","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/WedderburnConstruction.lean#L84-L90","doc":"On a single block, with matching multiplicity index, the assembly returns the\nblock's own entry. This is the read-off `blockDiagonal_injective` uses. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Wedderburn.blockDiagonal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Wedderburn.blockDiagonal","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/WedderburnConstruction.lean#L72-L82","doc":"**Block-diagonal assembly, constructed.** The entry at `(λ, m, i), (μ, m', j)`\nis `x_λ i j` when the partitions and the multiplicity indices agree, and `0`\notherwise. No axiom, and no dimension identity: the target index type is the one\nthe decomposition naturally lives on. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Wedderburn.RegIndex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Wedderburn.RegIndex","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/WedderburnConstruction.lean#L66-L70","doc":"**The regular-representation index.** Each partition `λ ⊢ n` contributes\n`f^λ` copies of an `f^λ`-dimensional space, so the cardinality is `Σ_λ (f^λ)²`\n— the number RSK identifies with `n!`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}